From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:20:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: hand the guest a new texture zeroed

A guest allocates the pages behind a new texture zeroed, and expects to
read zeros from the texture until it writes it. The texture's own
storage is memory the host driver hands out again once another resource
has released it, with that resource's pixels still in it. A texture the
renderer leaves as it finds it therefore shows what an earlier one held,
which may have belonged to another guest process, and a pair of fresh
buffers differ although neither was written. Android's
BitmapTest#testSameAs_wrappedHardwareBuffer compares exactly such a pair.

Clear every level of a texture the renderer creates with glClearTexImage
and no data, when the driver offers it. A texture imported from an image
keeps the content it was imported with, and a compressed format cannot
be cleared this way.

The clear is queued on the GPU and costs the creating thread no more
than the creation did. Each level adds about a tenth of a millisecond
before the GPU has finished the texture, plus the bandwidth to fill it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
index 63cb62d7cdeeb76a02868e3c22d54cda1b58fbbe..3e2d06cd1bc78eae59de5fddb26afba880d79e07 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -9446,6 +9446,33 @@ vrend_resource_create(const struct vrend_renderer_resource_create_args *args)
    return gr;
 }
 
+/* The storage of a new texture is memory the host driver hands out again once
+ * another resource - possibly another guest process's - has released it, and
+ * the guest allocated zeroed pages for the same resource. Fill a texture the
+ * renderer created with zeros before the guest can read it, so the guest sees
+ * what it allocated and never another resource's pixels. An imported image
+ * keeps the content it was imported with.
+ */
+static void vrend_resource_zero_texture(struct vrend_resource *gr)
+{
+   const enum virgl_formats fmt = gr->base.format;
+   const GLenum format = tex_conv_table[fmt].glformat;
+   const GLenum type = tex_conv_table[fmt].gltype;
+
+   if (!has_feature(feat_clear_texture) ||
+       !has_bit(gr->storage_bits, VREND_STORAGE_GL_TEXTURE) ||
+       has_bit(gr->storage_bits, VREND_STORAGE_EGL_IMAGE) ||
+       util_format_is_compressed(fmt) || !format || !type)
+      return;
+
+   for (uint32_t level = 0; level <= gr->base.last_level; level++) {
+      if (vrend_state.use_gles)
+         glClearTexImageEXT(gr->gl_id, level, format, type, NULL);
+      else
+         glClearTexImage(gr->gl_id, level, format, type, NULL);
+   }
+}
+
 struct pipe_resource *
 vrend_renderer_resource_create(const struct vrend_renderer_resource_create_args *args,
                                void *image_oes)
@@ -9462,6 +9489,8 @@ vrend_renderer_resource_create(const struct vrend_renderer_resource_create_args
    } else {
       const enum virgl_formats format = gr->base.format;
       ret = vrend_resource_alloc_texture(gr, format, image_oes);
+      if (!ret && !image_oes)
+         vrend_resource_zero_texture(gr);
    }
 
    if (ret) {
